# The delayed ability "transform Aang at the beginning of the next upkeep" is about the Aang that made it. On turn 2 Bot2
# bolts Bot1's Ornithopter and the ability waits for Bot1's upkeep on turn 3. With it on the stack there, Bot1 flickers Aang
# with Ephemerate: the Aang that returns is a new object (CR 400.7), not the one the ability would transform, so it does
# nothing and the new Aang stays Aang, at the Crossroads (a 3/3). His enters ability looks at five Islands and puts nothing
# onto the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Aang, at the Crossroads
Ornithopter
Ephemerate
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Aang, at the Crossroads.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ephemerate.Cast(Aang, at the Crossroads)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Aang, at the Crossroads
Bot1.Battlefield.Aang, at the Crossroads.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Aang, at the Crossroads.Toughness = 3
Exile = Ephemerate
